        "reason-4": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "number": "4",
            "title": "\"BPA-free\" was never the same as plastic-free.",
            "body": "<p>The baby bottle industry has relied heavily on the phrase “BPA-free” because it sounds reassuring—but it only tells part of the story. The label simply means the bottle does not contain Bisphenol A, one specific chemical. It does not mean the plastic cannot break down or release microscopic particles when exposed to heat. A 2025 federal court ruling reinforced that distinction, finding that “BPA-free” only guarantees the absence of BPA, not the absence of microplastics. Parents were given a comforting label while the underlying plastic material remained largely unchanged.</p>"
          }
        },
        "image-5": {
          "type": "image",
